{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Defiled by harlotry.</b> Who was penetrated in intercourse forbidden to her by Israel, such as one liable to karet, or a natin, or a mamzer (Sifra; Yevamot 61)." "<b>A ḥalalah.</b> Who was born of those disqualified from the priesthood, such as the daughter of a widow from a high priest, or the daughter of a divorcee (and a ḥalutzah) from an ordinary priest; and likewise one who was profaned from the priesthood through intercourse with one of those disqualified for the priesthood (see Sifra, Kiddushin 77)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:32.451250455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}